{"type":"diagram","design":"P66_ARCH_FLOW","title":"Unified retail data platform architecture","lead":"BigQuery, Dataplex, and Looker form a cohesive, serverless analytics fabric on Google Cloud.","columns":[{"label":"North America ingestion","items":[{"title":"Multi-region data streams","text":"Ingest US, Canada, and Mexico retail feeds into a serverless cloud foundation."},{"title":"Cross-channel inputs","text":"Capture storefront, digital commerce, and enterprise resource feeds without intermediate staging servers."}]},{"label":"BigQuery and Dataplex core","items":[{"title":"Multi-region BigQuery storage","text":"Store petabyte-scale retail datasets in decoupled compute and storage zones."},{"title":"Dataplex governance fabric","text":"Apply centralized metadata cataloging, automated quality rules, and domain security policies."}]},{"label":"Looker semantic consumption","items":[{"title":"Governed LookML layer","text":"Standardize enterprise retail KPIs in a version-controlled modeling layer querying BigQuery directly."},{"title":"Omnichannel analytics apps","text":"Deliver trusted self-service dashboards and embedded insights to store and corporate teams."}]}],"links":["Multi-region ingestion","Governed in-place queries"],"notes":"This architecture unifies Best Buy's North American data estate across the US, Canada, and Mexico on Google Cloud. Multi-region ingestion feeds directly into BigQuery storage, while Dataplex enforces centralized metadata and quality governance across all retail domains. Looker sits directly on top of BigQuery to provide a governed semantic layer without moving data into external cubes.

