{"type":"cards","title":"Quorum and Cloud Witness setup","groups":[{"label":"Primary region voting nodes","items":[{"title":"Primary SQL node","text":"Voting cluster member (weight 1)","icon":"hex-bolt"},{"title":"Local secondary node","text":"Voting cluster member (weight 1)","icon":"hex-gear"}]},{"label":"Third-region witness","items":[{"title":"File share witness","text":"Tie-breaker vote in independent region","icon":"shield-cloud"}]},{"label":"Secondary region DR node","items":[{"title":"DR SQL replica","text":"Dynamic vote weight managed for WAN","icon":"gear-database"}]}],"callouts":["Primary region SQL Server nodes hold active quorum votes to arbitrate local zonal failovers immediately.","A file share witness hosted in a third independent Google Cloud region acts as the tie-breaker if one node or region is isolated.","Dynamic quorum and automated vote weight adjustments remove votes from isolated nodes to maintain cluster majority."],"notes":"To prevent split-brain conditions during network partitions, the Windows Server Failover Cluster uses a Node and File Share Majority quorum model. Placing the witness in an independent third Google Cloud region ensures the primary region retains quorum if the WAN link or secondary region fails.

Sources:
[3] Deploying a Multi-Region SQL Server Disaster Recovery Environment (Google Cloud Tutorials, 2026) https://cloud.google.com/architecture/deploying-sql-server-disaster-recovery-environment","fact_tags":[],"items":[{"title":"Isolated third-region witness","text":"Places a lightweight file share witness in an independent Google Cloud region to provide an unbiased quorum vote if network connectivity breaks between the main regions.","icon":"network"},{"title":"Dynamic quorum vote management","text":"Configures Windows Server Failover Clustering to automatically adjust node voting weights based on real-time health, preventing split-brain scenarios during unexpected maintenance or infrastructure failures.","icon":"automation"},{"title":"Automated primary failover prioritization","text":"Assigns full voting rights to primary region nodes and zero votes to secondary disaster recovery nodes, ensuring automatic failover stays local while regional switches remain controlled.","icon":"target"}],"center":"Quorum design","resolvedIcons":{},"reference":{"tag":"S66_CARDS_PHOTO_STRIP","slideNumber":null,"subtype":null,"layoutPattern":"","uiComponents":[],"background":"light","cardStyle":"panel","score":60,"fallback":false},"deckLibrary":"solution","cobrand":false,"clientLogo":false}

