{"type":"process","design":"S66_STEP_COLUMNS","title":"Database migration and low-downtime cutover plan","items":[{"title":"Seed full backup","tag":"DBA team","icon":"cloud-upload","text":"Stream compressed full database backups from the legacy environment to the Google Cloud Storage staging bucket and restore with NORECOVERY on the new primary node."},{"title":"Start log shipping","tag":"Automation","icon":"cloud-sync","text":"Initiate continuous transaction log shipping from the legacy SQL Server to the Google Cloud primary replica to keep target databases warm prior to cutover. This reduces sync delays."},{"title":"Sync distributed AG","tag":"DBA team","icon":"database-network","text":"Configure a Distributed Availability Group between the legacy cluster and the new Google Cloud AG, switching to synchronous commit right before the cutover window."},{"title":"Repoint DNS and verify","tag":"Network and app teams","icon":"globe","text":"Halt clinical application writes, confirm zero replication lag, cut over the Distributed AG, repoint Cloud DNS to the new listener, and validate EHR connectivity."}],"notes":"To migrate Contoso Health without extended downtime, the database team seeds initial backups via Cloud Storage, establishes continuous log shipping, and uses a Distributed Availability Group for final synchronization. Cutover only requires halting writes briefly to verify zero lag and repointing DNS to the new internal load balancer listener.

