{"type":"process","design":"S66_STEP_COLUMNS","title":"Runbook: Cross-region disaster recovery failover","lead":"Documented execution steps guarantee regional recovery within the target window.","items":[{"title":"Declare regional outage","tag":"Incident commander","icon":"shield-user","text":"Confirm a primary region blackout via Cloud Monitoring telemetry and joint escalation bridge consensus, authorizing execution of the cross-region disaster recovery runbook."},{"title":"Force quorum and failover","tag":"DBA team","icon":"code-refresh","text":"Execute the pre-staged PowerShell runbook on the secondary region node to force Windows cluster quorum and run T-SQL forced failover on the Availability Group."},{"title":"Verify database state","tag":"DBA team","icon":"shield-database","text":"Confirm the DR replica transitions to the primary role online, completes undo recovery phases, and passes automated consistency and metadata checks."},{"title":"Update DNS and validate","tag":"Network and app teams","icon":"cloud-wifi","text":"Verify multi-subnet listener IP binding in Cloud DNS, promote the secondary region internal load balancer, and run clinical application smoke tests."}],"notes":"Cross-region failover between Google Cloud regions using asynchronous replication requires manual or runbook-driven failover with forced quorum to prevent split-brain conditions. The multi-subnet WSFC architecture spanning both regions enables rapid IP switching and clinical application reconnection.

